"person_slug":"lee-rhiannon","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Linda Reynolds","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10835","person_slug":"linda-reynolds","vote":"no"},{"name":"Louise Pratt","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10714","person_slug":"louise-pratt","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Malarndirri McCarthy","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10855","person_slug":"malarndirri-mccarthy","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Marise Payne","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10509","person_slug":"marise-payne","vote":"no"},{"name":"Matthew Canavan","party":"LNP","person_id":"tvfy_10827","person_slug":"matthew-canavan","vote":"no"},{"name":"Michaelia Cash","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10707","person_slug":"michaelia-cash","vote":"no"},{"name":"Mitch Fifield","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10224","person_slug":"mitch-fifield","vote":"no"},{"name":"Nick McKim","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10841","person_slug":"nick-mckim","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Nigel Scullion","party":"Country Liberal Party","person_id":"tvfy_10569","person_slug":"nigel-scullion","vote":"no"},{"name":"Patrick Dodson","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10846","person_slug":"patrick-dodson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Peter Georgiou","party":"One Nation","person_id":"tvfy_10898","person_slug":"peter-georgiou","vote":"no"},{"name":"Peter Whish-Wilson","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10780","person_slug":"peter-whish-wilson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Rachel Siewert","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10584","person_slug":"rachel-siewert","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Rex Patrick","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10903","person_slug":"rex-patrick","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Richard Di Natale","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10755","person_slug":"richard-di-natale","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ryan","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10715","person_slug":"scott-ryan","vote":"no"},{"name":"Simon Birmingham","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10044","person_slug":"simon-birmingham","vote":"no"},{"name":"Slade Brockman","party":"DPRES","person_id":"tvfy_10900","person_slug":"slade-brockman","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stirling Griff","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10851","person_slug":"stirling-griff","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sue Lines","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10782","person_slug":"sue-lines","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Motions - Broadband - Make NBN work","noes":25,"question":"The majority voted in favour of a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?id=2017-12-04.161.1) condemning the Government's approach to the National Broadband Network (NBN). Motions like these don't have legal force but can be influential as they represent the will of the Senate. ### Motion text > *That the Senate—* > *(a) notes that:* >> *(i) the Prime Minister is responsible for the decision to abandon optical fibre and instead deploy a second-rate National Broadband Network (NBN),* >> *(ii) NBN Co abandoned use of the Optus Hybrid Fibre Coaxial (HFC) infrastructure because it was deemed not fit for purpose,* >> *(iii) NBN Co has announced the company will immediately halt the HFC rollout because the technology is delivering poor service quality,* >> *(iv) NBN Co has indicated up to 2 million homes could have their NBN connection delayed by 6 to 9 months because of the mismanagement of the HFC rollout, and* >> *(v) it is nearly 2018 and the NBN still does not work properly; and* > *(b) calls on the Minister for Communications to:* >> *(i) stop attacking the Australian Broadcasting Corporation, and instead focus on making the NBN work, and* >> *(ii) apologise to the 48 000 households and small businesses in the electorate of Bennelong who are currently scheduled to be served by the unreliable HFC network.*","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-5033","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2017-12-04/8"}
